Q3: We have the Staff entity that uses multiple SharedEntityIdentiers:\par
\cf1\f3\fs19     [SharedSourceSystemIdentifiers(\par
        \cf3 typeof\cf1 (SchoolObjectModel),\par
        \cf3 typeof\cf1 (PowerSchool.PowerSchool),\par
        \cf3 typeof\cf1 (HumanResources.HumanResources),\par
        \cf3 typeof\cf1 (Json.Json))]\cf0\f0\fs22\par
Running the Poweschool Staff integration (Used only to allow FK checks for the SectionTeacher migrator to only insert if the staff exists.) caused 34 "Referred for manual deduplication:".\par
The  Staff.EmployeeId is the deduplication key and the starbridge database did not have any mappings to the Staff under the Powerschool Source system. It did have one for that staff for HRAd and SchoolObjectModel.\par
Jon suggested in a test env, to drop the Powerschool entry from the list of sharedSourceSystemIdentifiers. This worked and there were no manual deduplications picked up. I then added it back and it stayed working.\par
Jons concern was we could have a new Powerschool staff and it could show the same symtom. He determined there were some orphaned mappings that we underlying this issue and provided a script to clear them:\par
\par
\cf3\f1\fs19 DECLARE\cf1  @RC \cf3 int\cf1\par
\cf3 DECLARE\cf1  @MappingId \cf3 uniqueidentifier\cf2 ;\cf1\par
\cf3 DECLARE\cf1  @NotFoundEntities \cf3 TABLE\cf1\par
\cf2 (\cf1\par
\tab MappingId \cf3 uniqueidentifier\cf1\par
\cf2 )\cf1\par
\par
\cf3 insert\cf1  \cf3 into\cf1  @NotFoundEntities\cf3  \cf2 (\cf1  MappingId \cf2 )\cf1\par
\cf3 select\cf1  \cf3 distinct\cf1  m\cf2 .\cf1 Id \cf4 -- select *\cf1\par
\cf3 FROM\cf1  [StarBridge-Stdnt]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [Mapping] m\par
              \cf2 INNER\cf1  \cf2 JOIN\cf1  [StarBridge-Stdnt]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [SourceSystemEntityIdentity] ssei\par
                     \cf3 ON\cf1  m\cf2 .\cf1 [SourceSystemEntityIdentityId] \cf2 =\cf1  ssei\cf2 .\cf1 [Id]\par
              \cf2 INNER\cf1  \cf2 JOIN\cf1  [StarBridge-Stdnt]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [EntityType] et \cf3 ON\cf1  ssei\cf2 .\cf1 [EntityTypeId] \cf2 =\cf1  et\cf2 .\cf1 [Id]\par
              \cf2 INNER\cf1  \cf2 JOIN\cf1  [StarBridge-Stdnt]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [ExternalSystem] es \cf3 ON\cf1  ssei\cf2 .\cf1 [SourceSystemId] \cf2 =\cf1  es\cf2 .\cf1 [Id]\par
              \cf2 INNER\cf1  \cf2 JOIN\cf1  [StarBridge-Stdnt]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [DestinationSystemEntityIdentifier] dsei\par
                     \cf3 ON\cf1  m\cf2 .\cf1 [DestinationSystemEntityIdentifierId] \cf2 =\cf1  dsei\cf2 .\cf1 [Id]\par
              \cf2 LEFT\cf1  \cf2 OUTER\cf1  \cf2 JOIN\cf1  [DDH]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [Staff] s_on_id\par
                     \cf3 ON\cf1  dsei\cf2 .\cf1 [DestinationSystemEntityId] \cf2 =\cf1  s_on_id\cf2 .\cf1 [Id]\par
              \cf2 INNER\cf1  \cf2 JOIN\cf1  [DDH]\cf2 .\cf1 [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [Staff] s_on_employeeId\par
                     \cf3 ON\cf1  ssei\cf2 .\cf1 [SourceSystemEntityId] \cf2 =\cf1  s_on_employeeId\cf2 .\cf1 [EmployeeId]\par
       \cf3 WHERE\cf1  et\cf2 .\cf1 [Name] \cf2 =\cf1  \cf5 'Staff'\cf1  \cf2 AND\cf1  m\cf2 .\cf1 [State] \cf2 <>\cf1  3\par
              \cf2 AND\cf1  s_on_id\cf2 .\cf1 [Id] \cf2 IS\cf1  \cf2 NULL\cf1\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\cf3 DECLARE\cf1  cur \cf3 CURSOR\cf1  \cf3 FOR\cf1  \cf3 SELECT\cf1  MappingId \cf3 FROM\cf1  @NotFoundEntities\par
\cf3 DECLARE\cf1  @operationId \cf3 uniqueidentifier\cf2 ,\cf1\par
@timestamp \cf3 datetime\cf2 ;\cf1\par
\par
\cf3 OPEN\cf1  cur\par
\cf3 FETCH\cf1  \cf3 NEXT\cf1  \cf3 FROM\cf1  cur \cf3 INTO\cf1  @MappingId\par
\cf3 WHILE\cf1  \cf7 @@FETCH_STATUS\cf1  \cf2 =\cf1  0 \cf3 BEGIN\cf1\par
  \cf3 SET\cf1  @operationId \cf2 =\cf1  \cf7 NEWID\cf2 ();\cf1\par
  \cf3 SET\cf1  @timestamp \cf2 =\cf1  \cf7 GETDATE\cf2 ();\cf1\par
  \cf3 PRINT\cf1  \cf7 convert\cf2 (\cf3 varchar\cf2 (\cf1 36\cf2 ),\cf1  @MappingId\cf2 )+\cf1  \cf5 ', '\cf1  \cf2 +\cf1  \cf7 convert\cf2 (\cf3 varchar\cf2 (\cf1 36\cf2 ),\cf1  @operationId\cf2 )\cf1  \cf2 +\cf1  \cf5 ', '\cf1  \cf2 +\cf1  \cf7 convert\cf2 (\cf3 varchar\cf2 (\cf1 36\cf2 ),\cf1  @timestamp\cf2 )\cf1\par
  \cf3 EXECUTE\cf1  @RC \cf2 =\cf1  [dbo]\cf2 .\cf1 [SetMappingState]\cf3     \cf1 @MappingId\cf2 ,\cf1  @operationId\cf2 ,\cf1  @timestamp\cf2 ,\cf1  3\par
  \cf3 FETCH\cf1  \cf3 NEXT\cf1  \cf3 FROM\cf1  cur \cf3 INTO\cf1  @MappingId\par
\cf3 END\cf1\par
\par
\cf3 CLOSE\cf1  cur\par
\cf3 DEALLOCATE\cf1  cur\cf0\f0\fs22\par
\par
This cleared the mapings (State=3) and seems to have fixed the issue. \par
