Q4: How can I debug an Ifeed:\par
Launch Starbridge from the console (as on prod server) and attach the debugger to the Visual Studio project using it. \par
You can also print out the loadEntities collection to a json file as: \par
\cf3\f3\fs19 using\cf1  System.Text.Json;\par
        \cf3 public\cf1  IEntityCollection<Staff> LoadEntities()\par
        \{\par
            \cf3 using\cf1  \cf3 var\cf1  context =\par
                \cf3 this\cf1 .schoolObjectModelContextFactory.CreateSchoolObjectModelContext();\par
            \cf3 var\cf1  x =\par
                context\par
                .Staff\par
                .Where(staff =>\par
                    staff.SourceKey == 1 &&\par
                    staff.DeletedTimestamp == \cf3 null\cf1  &&\par
                    (staff.DeactivatedDate == \cf3 null\cf1  ||\par
                     staff.DeactivatedDate > DateTime.Now))\par
                .ToArray()\par
                .Select(\par
                    staff => \cf3 new\cf1  Staff()\par
                    \{\par
                        EmployeeId = staff.EmployeeId,\par
                    \});\par
\par
            \cf3 var\cf1  res = x;\par
            \cf3 var\cf1  stringOFJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(res);\par
            File.WriteAllText(\cf8 @"c:\\temp\\iFeedString.json"\cf1 , stringOFJson);\par
\par
            \cf3 return\cf1  x.ToEntityCollection();\par
        \}\par
\cf0\f0\fs22\par
